/**

@page applications_exahype2_gravity_waves Gravity waves

We also consider a model problem for atmospheric gravity waves using the ExaHyPE2 framework. The goal of this setup is to simulate the
propagation of gravity waves in a vertically stratified, compressible atmosphere, including the interaction between
fluid dynamics and basic thermo-chemical processes in the upper atmosphere.
This provides a multi-physics benchmark combining fluid flow, diffusion, and
atmospheric chemistry within the same adaptive, hyperbolic PDE framework.

The atmospheric background state is constructed from tabulated atmospheric profiles stored
in a CSV file. For each grid point, the code samples the CSV data as a function of height and
interpolates between adjacent rows to obtain a smoothly stratified initial condition.
From this table, the model reads the mass density, temperature, and number densities of the
major neutral species: atomic oxygen \f$ (\text{O}) \f$ , molecular oxygen \f$ (\text{O}_2) \f$, nitrogen \f$ (\text{N}_2) \f$,
and optionally hydrogen \f$ (\text{H}) \f$.

# Scenarios

\li \subpage applications_exahype2_airglow
\li \subpage applications_exahype2_thunderstorm

*/
